INT. BAYVIEW DINER - BOOTH - NIGHT

Empty except for one booth. Rain on the window. Fry oil smell.

YUSUF, 30s, sits stiffly with his hands in his lap. BEA, 30s, slides in opposite. LENNY, 60s, their father, shuffles over with a coffee pot.

BEA
Yusuf. You came.

YUSUF
You said Dad was sick.

LENNY
Not sick. Old.

BEA
Lenny, sit down.

LENNY
It's my diner.

YUSUF
(rising)
Then why is it for sale?

Lenny sets the pot down. It rattles.

LENNY
Because your sister doesn't want it.

BEA
Because you were never going to give it to him!

Yusuf stands. Bea grabs his wrist.

BEA (CONT'D)
Yusuf. Please.

He sits. Lenny pours coffee, three cups, his hand steady.

LENNY
Eat something, both of you.
